{{Infobox galaxy|name=Grus ll|constellation name=[[Grus (constellation)|Grus]]|ra=331.02|dec=-46.44|dist_ly=179,386 ly|group_cluster=Milky Way subgroup}}

'''Grus ll''' is an ultra-faint [[dwarf galaxy]] (UFD) located at a distance of 55 kiloparsecs from the [[Milky Way]] in the [[constellation]] of [[Grus (constellation)|Grus]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Martínez-Vázquez |first1=C. E. |last2=Vivas |first2=A. K. |last3=Gurevich |first3=M. |last4=Walker |first4=A. R. |last5=McCarthy |first5=M. |last6=Pace |first6=A. B. |last7=Stringer |first7=K. M. |last8=Santiago |first8=B. |last9=Hounsell |first9=R. |last10=Macri |first10=L. |last11=Li |first11=T. S. |last12=Bechtol |first12=K. |last13=Riley |first13=A. H. |last14=Kim |first14=A. G. |last15=Simon |first15=J. D. |date=December 2019 |title=Search for RR Lyrae stars in DES ultrafaint systems: Grus I, Kim 2, Phoenix II, and Grus II |journal=Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society |language=en |volume=490 |issue=2 |pages=2183–2199 |doi=10.1093/mnras/stz2609 |bibcode=2019MNRAS.490.2183M |doi-access=free |issn=0035-8711|arxiv=1909.06308 }}</ref>

It has a higher than expected ratio of [<nowiki/>[[Magnesium|Mg]]/[[Calcium|Ca]]] than other [[Metal-poor star|metal poor stars]] in ultra-diffuse galaxies. The chemical enrichment of Grus ll is from the [[stellar nucleosynthesis]] of [[Core-collapse supernova|core collapse supernovas]] from high mass [[star]]s over 20 solar masses and the [[Neutron star merger|merging]] of [[neutron star]]s. The stars within Grus ll may also possess a small enhancement of [[R-process|rapid neutron capture]] (r-process) elements.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Hansen |first1=T. T. |last2=Marshall |first2=J. L. |last3=Simon |first3=J. D. |last4=Li |first4=T. S. |last5=Bernstein |first5=R. A. |last6=Pace |first6=A. B. |last7=Ferguson |first7=P. |last8=Nagasawa |first8=D. Q. |last9=Kuehn |first9=K. |last10=Carollo |first10=D. |last11=Geha |first11=M. |last12=James |first12=D. |last13=Walker |first13=A. |last14=Diehl |first14=H. T. |last15=Aguena |first15=M. |date=July 2020 |title=Chemical Analysis of the Ultrafaint Dwarf Galaxy Grus II. Signature of High-mass Stellar Nucleosynthesis |journal=The Astrophysical Journal |language=en |volume=897 |issue=2 |pages=183 |doi=10.3847/1538-4357/ab9643 |bibcode=2020ApJ...897..183H |doi-access=free |issn=0004-637X|arxiv=2005.10767 }}</ref>

